ampus Life Career Development Job preparation - just for Jackets We’re here to help you with everything from resume composition to interviewing skills. The Career Development team, located in the Pathways Center, offer assistance as you work to find your dream job. Alumni and current students can search for thousands of jobs and internship postings, attend career development events, and get hired through Handshake. Contact Our Team Student Work Study Qualifying students are eligible for Federal Work Study jobs across campus where they can balance working part time while participating in athletics and prioritizing their studies. Learn More About Work Study Career Fair Payment Form Registration is required before payment is submitted for upcoming career fairs. To find out which career fairs are being offered this semester, email Sarah Bell at sbell@waynesburg.edu. Connect on Handshake Current Students Create a profile, apply for jobs and internships, attend events, and get hired! Log in through myConnect Employers Create an account, post jobs, connect with the Career office, and recruit Waynesburg University students! Connect with WU Alumni & Community Learn more about all that Handshake has to offer and create an account! Get started What We Offer Services Available For Students Grow your career potential with the help of our services such as: Handshake (Job & Internship Board) Vocation Exploration Assessments On- and off-campus job and internship fairs Employer networking opportunities Workshops One-on-one career coaching Mock interviewing Resume and cover letter review Assistance with graduate school applications and practice exams Career Closet (free professional clothing for University students) Employer Opportunities Career Connections Become an official Career Connections partner to have your recruiter contact information posted on Waynesburg University's internal job and internship leads board. Career Connections partners: Gain exclusive access to virtual and on-campus events, like job and internship fairs, tabling, and information sessions. Are able to post openings internally for students to review (email them to pathways@waynesburg.edu) May become an Internship Partner of Waynesburg University. Can work collaboratively with Waynesburg's Career Development Office to benefit both your organization/company and Waynesburg University students throughout the recruiting process. Click here to become a Career Connections Partner Join Us on Handshake Connect with us on Handshake to post job opportunities, register for events, schedule on-campus interviews, and recruit Waynesburg University Students. Handshake is the No. 1 way for college students to find jobs, and the most accessible way for employers to connect with Waynesburg students. Click here to learn more and join - or log in and connect with us! Memberships Waynesburg University is a member of PERC and the Accounting & Finance Consortium. Meet our students at these Pittsburgh-area events! Part of the Pathways Center The Pathways Center is an initiative to provide comprehensive student support services including Tutoring, Disability Services, Student Success Services, Career Development, Vocational Exploration, MUM System, Student Work Study Program, Library Services, the Writing Center, the Act 101 Educational Enrichment Program and more.  The Pathways Center is located in Eberly Library with collaborative referrals to and work with the Counseling Center, Student Services, Center for Entrepreneurial Leadership, Alumni Relations, Athletics, academic programs and others. Email our team at pathways@waynesburg.edu . Next Steps Contact our team to inquire about services, receive resume assistance, apply for federal work study, and more. Employers can contact us at pathways@waynesburg.edu to learn more about networking opportunities and upcoming events. Review related programs & request support Learn More about the Pathways Center 51 West College Street Waynesburg, PA 15370 